 "text": "Many of us work for hours without a break. We think it helps us finish faster. In fact, the opposite is often true. After a long stretch, our attention starts to drift. We look at the same line twice and make small errors. A short break can reset the mind. Stand up, stretch and look out of a window. Walk to the kitchen and pour a glass of water. Five minutes is often enough. Some people work for fifty minutes and then rest for ten. Find a rhythm that suits you. Your work will be better, and your day will feel lighter. Try it for a week and compare."
